# LOTUS vocabulary for RDF Portal.
#
# 48 terms (4 classes, 44 properties) describing the graph that
# lotus_csv_to_rdf.py builds from the LOTUS frozen CSV export. The converter
# emits this file into the SAME named graph as the instance data
# (<http://rdfportal.org/dataset/lotus>) and does so by default, so a
# conversion cannot ship data without the vocabulary that explains it.
#
# Why the same graph: every TogoMCP query pins its graph. A vocabulary in a
# second graph is invisible under that pin — schema discovery through SPARQL
# would return 0 rows and an agent would conclude the properties are
# undocumented. RDF Portal's `taxonomy` graph carries its DDBJ TBox inline the
# same way. 290 triples against 9.1 M is not a cost.
#
# Why a separate FILE: this is hand-authored prose reviewed once by DBCLS and
# the LOTUS team, while the instance data is re-converted per release. A typo
# fixed here must not cost a 100 s re-conversion of a 1.3 GB file.
#
# TURTLE SUBSET: the converter parses this file with a deliberately small
# reader (stdlib only, no rdflib). Supported: @prefix, `a`, IRIs, prefixed
# names, plain/long/typed/language literals, `;` and `,` lists. NOT supported:
# blank nodes, `[]`, collections, numeric and boolean shorthand, @base. The
# reader raises a TurtleSubsetError naming the line rather than guessing, so
# keep edits inside the subset — or re-render with `rapper -i turtle`.
#
# Coverage percentages are v11 (2026-04-13), per entity, not per CSV row.

@prefix lotus:   <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus#> .
@prefix owl:     <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:     <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:     <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix vann:    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/> .

########################################################################
# Ontology header
########################################################################

<http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus>
    a owl:Ontology ;
    dcterms:title "LOTUS vocabulary" ;
    dcterms:description """Classes and properties for LOTUS referenced structure-organism
occurrences of natural products, as hosted by RDF Portal. Versioned independently of the
LOTUS data release: this vocabulary is 1.0 whatever release the graph holds, and the release
is stated by pav:version on <http://rdfportal.org/dataset/lotus>.""" ;
    owl:versionInfo "1.0" ;
    vann:preferredNamespacePrefix "lotus" ;
    vann:preferredNamespaceUri "http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus#" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://lotus.nprod.net/> ;
    rdfs:comment """No property is declared owl:FunctionalProperty except the three links out of
lotus:Occurrence, which are single-valued by construction (an occurrence IRI is minted from
exactly one structure, organism and reference QID). The omission elsewhere is deliberate, not an
oversight: lotus:inchikey and the three lotus:npclassifier* properties are genuinely repeatable,
and asserting functionality on them would license a reasoner to merge distinct values.""" .

########################################################################
# Classes
########################################################################

lotus:Occurrence
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Occurrence" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment """A report that one chemical structure was found in one organism, documented by
one literature reference (672,413 in v11). This is the unit of assertion in LOTUS, and a
first-class node rather than a structure-to-organism edge because the reference is the evidence,
not decoration: the same structure-organism pair is typically reported by several papers.
Occurrence IRIs are the only minted ones in the graph, built deterministically from the three
Wikidata QIDs as <http://rdfportal.org/dataset/lotus/occurrence/QSTRUCT_QORG_QREF>, so
re-converting a release reproduces them byte for byte and two releases can be diffed directly.""" .

lotus:Structure
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Structure" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment """A chemical structure of a natural product (227,256 in v11). Identified by its
Wikidata IRI (http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q...), not a minted one, so the graph joins to
Wikidata and to IDSM's Wikidata compound mirror with no mapping table. Carries skos:exactMatch to
an http://rdf.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubchem/compound/CID... IRI on 97.3% of structures.""" .

lotus:Organism
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Organism" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment """An organism a natural product was reported from (37,486 in v11). Identified by
its Wikidata IRI. Carries skos:exactMatch to http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/<taxid> on 78.0% (see
lotus:ncbiTaxonId for what that costs a join) and rdfs:seeAlso to a GBIF species page on 98.1%.
The ten rank properties lotus:taxonDomain..lotus:taxonVarietas hold NAMES, not IRIs, because that
is all the source CSV has, and their coverage is uneven by rank (97.2% down to 0.7%). For real
hierarchy traversal, join skos:exactMatch into RDF Portal's `taxonomy` database and walk
rdfs:subClassOf* there: LOTUS supplies occurrences, `taxonomy` supplies the tree.""" .

lotus:Reference
    a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Reference" ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment """A publication reporting an occurrence (91,426 in v11). Identified by its
Wikidata IRI. The DOI is the complete identifier here and the PMID is the joinable one:
rdfs:seeAlso reaches https://doi.org/<doi> for essentially every reference, while skos:exactMatch
to PubMed exists for only 47.1%. Everything beyond the DOI (title, date, PMID, PMCID, venue) is
absent from the frozen CSV and folded in from a Wikidata export by the converter's --refs-nt
option; a graph built without it has references carrying a DOI and nothing else.""" .

########################################################################
# Occurrence properties
########################################################################

lotus:structure
    a owl:ObjectProperty, owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:label "structure" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Occurrence ;
    rdfs:range lotus:Structure ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "The structure reported by this occurrence. Exactly one." .

lotus:organism
    a owl:ObjectProperty, owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:label "organism" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Occurrence ;
    rdfs:range lotus:Organism ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "The organism the structure was reported from. Exactly one." .

lotus:reference
    a owl:ObjectProperty, owl:FunctionalProperty ;
    rdfs:label "reference" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Occurrence ;
    rdfs:range lotus:Reference ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "The publication reporting this occurrence. Exactly one." .

lotus:manuallyValidated
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "manually validated" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Occurrence ;
    rdfs:range xsd:boolean ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment """True when LOTUS curators manually validated this occurrence (178 of 672,413 in
v11). ABSENT MEANS NOT CHECKED, NOT FALSE. The source records "NA" for everything else, so
emitting false would assert something the source does not say, and the property is therefore
emitted only when true. A query for unvalidated occurrences must test for ABSENCE
(FILTER NOT EXISTS / OPTIONAL + !BOUND), never for the value false, which matches nothing.""" .

########################################################################
# Structure properties
########################################################################

lotus:inchikey
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "InChIKey" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Structure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment """InChIKey of the structure. 100%. REPEATABLE in rare cases: 87 structure QIDs
carry more than one InChIKey in v11 (at most 3), and the converter emits all of them rather than
silently choosing. Anything keying on InChIKey should expect that, and this is why the property is
not declared functional.""" .

lotus:inchi
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "InChI" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Structure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Full InChI string. 100%." .

lotus:smiles
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "SMILES" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Structure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Isomeric SMILES, i.e. stereochemistry retained. 100%. See lotus:smiles2D for the flat form." .

lotus:smiles2D
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "2D SMILES" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Structure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment """Flat SMILES with stereochemistry stripped. 100%. The right key for matching
across sources that disagree about stereochemistry; lotus:smiles is the right one for identity.""" .

lotus:molecularFormula
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "molecular formula" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Structure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Molecular formula in Hill order, e.g. \"C37H66O7\". 100%. A string: compare it literally, do not parse it for arithmetic." .

lotus:exactMass
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "exact mass" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Structure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Monoisotopic exact mass in daltons. 100%. Typed xsd:decimal, so numeric range filters work directly." .

lotus:xlogp
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "XLogP" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Structure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:decimal ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Computed octanol-water partition coefficient. 99.7%." .

lotus:iupacName
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "IUPAC name" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Structure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Systematic IUPAC name. 96.6%." .

lotus:traditionalName
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "traditional name" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Structure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment """Common or trivial name, e.g. "(+)-Annonacin". 96.9%, and also emitted as
rdfs:label — so 3.1% of structures have no label at all and a query joining on rdfs:label drops
them. Use OPTIONAL unless you mean to filter.""" .

lotus:stereocenterCount
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "stereocenter count" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Structure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Total number of stereocenters. 100%." .

lotus:unspecifiedStereocenterCount
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "unspecified stereocenter count" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Structure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:integer ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment """Number of stereocenters whose configuration is not specified. 100%. Zero here
means the structure is fully resolved stereochemically; a non-zero value means the SMILES is
partially ambiguous.""" .

lotus:npclassifierPathway
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "NPClassifier pathway" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Structure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment """Biosynthetic pathway from NPClassifier, e.g. "Polyketides". 97.1%. REPEATABLE:
a compound of mixed biosynthetic origin carries several. The source packs them into one CSV cell
as "Fatty acids $ Polyketides" (up to 11.6% of rows) and the converter splits them, so a filter on
one value also matches co-classified compounds — which is correct, and the opposite of what the
raw CSV gives you.""" .

lotus:npclassifierSuperclass
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "NPClassifier superclass" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Structure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Superclass from NPClassifier. 91.5%. REPEATABLE, see lotus:npclassifierPathway." .

lotus:npclassifierClass
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "NPClassifier class" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Structure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Class from NPClassifier, the most specific of its three levels. 88.6%. REPEATABLE, see lotus:npclassifierPathway." .

lotus:classyfireKingdom
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "ClassyFire kingdom" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Structure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment """Kingdom in the ClassyFire chemical taxonomy. 98.6%. ClassyFire and NPClassifier
are two independent classifications of the same structure, not two levels of one: ClassyFire is
structural, NPClassifier is biosynthetic. Do not mix their levels in one rollup.""" .

lotus:classyfireSuperclass
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "ClassyFire superclass" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Structure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Superclass in the ClassyFire chemical taxonomy. 98.6%." .

lotus:classyfireClass
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "ClassyFire class" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Structure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Class in the ClassyFire chemical taxonomy. 97.9%." .

lotus:classyfireDirectParent
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "ClassyFire direct parent" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Structure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Most specific ClassyFire term assigned to the structure. 83.2% — notably sparser than the three levels above it." .

lotus:chemontId
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "ChemOnt ID" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Structure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment """ClassyFire ChemOnt identifier in canonical zero-padded form, e.g.
"CHEMONTID:0002518". 98.6%. Deliberately a literal rather than an IRI: ChemOnt has no agreed
resolvable IRI namespace. If one is adopted this becomes an object property and connects to
ontology tooling.""" .

lotus:pubchemCompoundId
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "PubChem compound ID" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Structure ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment """PubChem CID as a bare literal, e.g. "441555". 97.3%. The same link is emitted
as skos:exactMatch to the http://rdf.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubchem/compound/CID... IRI; use that form
to join the `pubchem` database, and this one only to display or match the number.""" .

########################################################################
# Organism properties
########################################################################

lotus:scientificName
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "scientific name" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Organism ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Scientific name of the organism, e.g. \"Annona muricata\". 100%, and also emitted as rdfs:label." .

lotus:gbifTaxonId
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "GBIF taxon ID" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Organism ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "GBIF taxon key. 98.1% — the best-covered of the three taxonomy ids. Also emitted as rdfs:seeAlso to the GBIF species page." .

lotus:ncbiTaxonId
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "NCBI taxon ID" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Organism ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment """NCBI Taxonomy id. 78.0% of organisms — the lowest-covered identifier on this
class, and the trap on this graph: a join into RDF Portal's `taxonomy` database through
skos:exactMatch silently drops 8,252 organisms, with no error and a plausible-looking result.
Prefer lotus:gbifTaxonId (98.1%) or lotus:ottTaxonId (97.8%) when completeness matters more than
reaching the NCBI tree, and say which one an answer used. Per CSV ROW the figure looks like 86.6%
because well-studied organisms recur in many rows; 78.0% per entity is the honest number.""" .

lotus:ottTaxonId
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "OTT taxon ID" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Organism ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Open Tree of Life taxonomy id. 97.8%." .

lotus:taxonDomain
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "domain" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Organism ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Name of the organism's domain. One of ten flat rank properties holding names, not IRIs; see lotus:Organism for what that means for rollups." .

lotus:taxonKingdom
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "kingdom" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Organism ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Name of the organism's kingdom. See lotus:Organism for the rank-coverage caveat." .

lotus:taxonPhylum
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "phylum" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Organism ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Name of the organism's phylum. See lotus:Organism for the rank-coverage caveat." .

lotus:taxonClass
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "class (taxonomic)" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Organism ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Name of the organism's taxonomic class. Unrelated to the ClassyFire and NPClassifier `class` properties on lotus:Structure. See lotus:Organism for the rank-coverage caveat." .

lotus:taxonOrder
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "order" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Organism ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Name of the organism's order. See lotus:Organism for the rank-coverage caveat." .

lotus:taxonFamily
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "family" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Organism ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Name of the organism's family, e.g. \"Annonaceae\". The most useful rank for a biosynthetic rollup. See lotus:Organism for the rank-coverage caveat." .

lotus:taxonTribe
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "tribe" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Organism ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Name of the organism's tribe. 44.7% — absence is unknown, not exclusion, so grouping on this rank hides more than half the organisms." .

lotus:taxonGenus
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "genus" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Organism ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Name of the organism's genus. See lotus:Organism for the rank-coverage caveat." .

lotus:taxonSpecies
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "species" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Organism ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Name of the organism's species. See lotus:Organism for the rank-coverage caveat." .

lotus:taxonVarietas
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "varietas" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Organism ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Name of the organism's variety. 0.7% — the sparsest rank in the graph; treat it as incidental detail, never as a grouping key." .

########################################################################
# Reference properties
#
# Everything except lotus:doi comes from the Wikidata export folded in by the
# converter's --refs-nt option. Without it, a reference has a DOI and nothing
# else; the coverage figures below all assume it was used.
########################################################################

lotus:doi
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "DOI" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Reference ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment """DOI as a bare literal, e.g. "10.1055/S-2003-38485". 99.96% (91,386 of 91,426)
and the only reference attribute present in the frozen CSV itself. Also emitted as rdfs:seeAlso to
https://doi.org/<doi>, percent-encoded — thousands of Wiley DOIs contain < and >, which would
otherwise terminate the IRI.""" .

lotus:title
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "title" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Reference ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "Title of the publication. 99.7%, --refs-nt only, and also emitted as rdfs:label." .

lotus:publicationDate
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "publication date" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Reference ;
    rdfs:range xsd:date ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment """Date of publication, truncated from Wikidata's dateTime to xsd:date. 99.1%,
--refs-nt only. Wikidata records an unknown month or day as 01, so a date is reliable to the year
and no further.""" .

lotus:pmid
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "PubMed ID" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Reference ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment """PubMed identifier. 47.1%, --refs-nt only. Fewer than half the references carry
one, so a join to RDF Portal's `pubmed` database reaches at most 43,075 of the 91,426 papers —
that is a property of the literature, not a defect to work around. Also emitted as skos:exactMatch
to http://rdf.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/<pmid>.""" .

lotus:pmcid
    a owl:DatatypeProperty ;
    rdfs:label "PMC ID" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Reference ;
    rdfs:range xsd:string ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment "PubMed Central identifier. 5.0%, --refs-nt only. Too sparse to filter on; useful only opportunistically, to reach full text." .

lotus:publishedIn
    a owl:ObjectProperty ;
    rdfs:label "published in" ;
    rdfs:domain lotus:Reference ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdfportal.org/ontology/lotus> ;
    rdfs:comment """The journal, as a Wikidata IRI (http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q...). 99.2%,
--refs-nt only. No range is declared: the venue is a Wikidata entity that this graph does not
describe, so it carries no label here — resolve it against Wikidata or IDSM to name a journal.""" .
